        },
        {
          "id": "p2",
          "text": "The v2 specification defines payment requirements, a client payment payload and settlement responses, with facilitator interfaces for verification and settlement. Its HTTP transport uses PAYMENT-REQUIRED for requirements and PAYMENT-SIGNATURE for authorization. Scheme and network support must match the requested payment; the protocol's extensibility is not universal implementation compatibility. [1] [2]"
        },
        {
          "id": "p3",
          "text": "For an XRPL integration, I recommend documenting the exact supported scheme, network identifier, asset encoding and proof-validation rules. Reconcile the ledger transaction and actual delivery before declaring settlement successful. The partial-payment reference is relevant because requested amounts alone cannot safely establish received value. Keep premium access conditional on the application's verified delivery boundary rather than on an untrusted payment header. [1] [2]"
